That's right, this simple intervention closed 60% of the achievement gap. Educators have been struggling for decades to find ways to close this gap because it's one of the achievement gap. Educators have been struggling for decades to find ways to close this gap because it's one of the most persistent and disturbing disparities in American education. Now, I don't want to imply that this one intervention can fix the whole problem. Hunter's experiment is going to have to be replicated at other schools, with other students and other teachers, but I think the idea is really promising. It's inexpensive, it's easy, and it builds on top of a mountain of other research that finds strong relationships between students and teachers make a difference.
没错，这个简单的干预措施缩小了60%的成绩差距。几十年来，教育工作者一直在努力寻找缩小这种差距的方法，因为这是美国教育中最顽固、最令人不安的不平等现象之一。现在，我并不是暗示这单一的干预措施就能解决所有问题。亨特的实验还需要在其他学校、与其他学生和老师一起进行复制，但我认为这个想法真的很有前景。它成本低、操作简单，并且建立在大量其他研究的基础之上——这些研究发现，学生和老师之间紧密的联系能带来改变。

